<Layout title="MCP setup"><h1>Preflight in your tools.</h1><p class="intro">Use the repository’s local MCP server when mcp/ is available. GitHub Pages serves files and cannot run an MCP server.</p><section><h2>Build the local server</h2><p>The mcp/ implementation is not present in this worktree yet. The following setup assumes its package provides a build script and dist/index.js entry point; check mcp/README.md before using it.</p><pre><code>git clone https://github.com/legacy-ev/preflight.git
cd preflight/mcp
npm ci
npm run build</code></pre><h2>Claude Desktop configuration</h2><p>In Claude Desktop, open Settings → Developer → Edit Config. Add the server under mcpServers, replace the absolute paths, save and restart Claude Desktop.</p><pre><code>{JSON.stringify({mcpServers:{preflight:{command:'/absolute/path/to/node',args:['/absolute/path/to/preflight/mcp/dist/index.js']}}},null,2)}</code></pre><p><a href="https://modelcontextprotocol.io/docs/develop/connect-local-servers">Official MCP local-server guide</a></p><p>Typical config file: ~/Library/Application Support/Claude/claude_desktop_config.json on macOS, or %APPDATA%\Claude\claude_desktop_config.json on Windows. Node 20 is required by this repository.</p><p>Look for the preflight tool after restart. If absent, check server logs and the actual entry point in mcp/package.json. Static mode supports read snapshots; report_outcome is not a live ingest service. Never give the server payment or account credentials.</p><p><a href="https://github.com/legacy-ev/preflight/tree/main/mcp">MCP source and setup instructions →</a></p></section></Layout>
